# DESIGN.md

<!--
  Template for a third-party project's root DESIGN.md.

  This repo (mountain-pass/design-framework) is the source of truth for this
  project's design system. Copy this file into the target project's repo root
  as `DESIGN.md`, fill in the placeholders below, and delete this comment.

  Placeholders:
    {{DESIGN}}  - design folder name, e.g. slate, warm-paper
    {{LAYOUT}}  - layout folder name, e.g. app-shell, document-editor
    {{REF}}     - branch, tag, or commit in design-framework, e.g. main
-->

This project's design system lives in a separate repo:
[mountain-pass/design-framework](https://github.com/mountain-pass/design-framework).

Use the `{{DESIGN}}` design and the `{{LAYOUT}}` layout from that repo. Before
styling or building any UI, fetch and read these files in full:

```
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mountain-pass/design-framework/{{REF}}/CLAUDE.md
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mountain-pass/design-framework/{{REF}}/shared/TOKENS.md
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mountain-pass/design-framework/{{REF}}/shared/COMPONENTS.md
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mountain-pass/design-framework/{{REF}}/designs/{{DESIGN}}/DESIGN.md
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mountain-pass/design-framework/{{REF}}/layouts/{{LAYOUT}}/LAYOUT.md
```

Also open the kitchen sink demo — it is the rendered answer to "what does this
component look like", not just a description of one:

```
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mountain-pass/design-framework/{{REF}}/designs/{{DESIGN}}/index.html
```

Copy the theme verbatim from:

```
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mountain-pass/design-framework/{{REF}}/designs/{{DESIGN}}/theme.css
```

## Rules

- Use semantic tokens only (`bg-background`, `text-muted-foreground`,
  `border-border`, ...). Never hard-code hex colours or Tailwind colour
  classes like `bg-blue-500`.
- The layout controls structure (regions, sizes, responsive behaviour, scroll
  model). The design controls appearance (colour, type, spacing, component
  styling). If they conflict on anything else, ask rather than guessing.
- Follow the "Never" list in the design's `DESIGN.md`. If a rule genuinely
  can't be followed, say why instead of silently breaking it.
- Both light and dark mode are part of the deliverable, not an afterthought.
